<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Asterias rubens Turing wavelength at 115.2 µm (Holocene, Pass 2) (Asterias rubens (common starfish), Holocene, 0 Ma)",
        "Asterias rubens Turing wavelength at 115.2 µm (Holocene, Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Asterias rubens (common starfish), Holocene, 0 Ma morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Asterias rubens (common starfish), Holocene, 0 Ma specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Asterias rubens (common starfish), Holocene, 0 Ma" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A second, independent assessor.",
        "does_not_claim: That 115.2 µm was measured on this specimen.",
        "does_not_claim: That the organism silhouette is the correct 576 µm domain. The control shows it quenches the mode.",
        "does_not_claim: That the studio photograph is a micrograph, or that its pixel scale is 115.2 µm.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: FTCS growth versus analytical σ(k), diffusivity sweep, equal-diffusion ablation.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Silhouette-domain quench control and a within-plate tubercle-spacing null.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: a=0.072, b=0.918, D_v/D_u=7.62, domain 576.0 µm = 5 × 115.2 µm, seed 3123.",
        "reported_in_source: Garm & Nilsson 2014: most starfish have a compound eye at the arm tip; their navigation experiments used Linckia laevigata.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981 writes the pre-pattern wavenumber used for animal markings.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 two-species reaction with a homogeneous steady state.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 115.2 µm length is the catalog tier, transferred onto Schnakenberg kinetics. It is not a published Asterias ocellus diameter.",
        "transfer_boundary: The Linckia compound-eye result is not an Asterias rubens wavelength." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Asterias rubens" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Ostrakoderma (Mollusca & Echinodermata)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Asterias" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/asterias_rubens_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Asterias rubens (common starfish), Holocene, 0 Ma; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species reaction with a homogeneous steady state. | Murray 1981 writes the pre-pattern wavenumber used for animal markings. | Garm & Nilsson 2014: most starfish have a compound eye at the arm tip; their navigation experiments used Linckia laevigata.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.072, b=0.918, D_v/D_u=7.62, domain 576.0 µm = 5 × 115.2 µm, seed 3123. | FTCS growth versus analytical σ(k), diffusivity sweep, equal-diffusion ablation. | Silhouette-domain quench control and a within-plate tubercle-spacing null.; transfer_boundary: The 115.2 µm length is the catalog tier, transferred onto Schnakenberg kinetics. It is not a published Asterias ocellus diameter. | The Linckia compound-eye result is not an Asterias rubens wavelength.; does_not_claim: That 115.2 µm was measured on this specimen. | That the studio photograph is a micrograph, or that its pixel scale is 115.2 µm. | That the organism silhouette is the correct 576 µm domain. The control shows it quenches the mode. | A second, independent assessor.]; phenomenon_size: 115 µm (0.0001152 m, log10=-3.939 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 115 µm to 36.0 cm): 115 µm:asterias-rubens-bioelectric-polarity, 430 µm:asterias-rubens-vertex-packing, 8.0 mm:asterias-rubens-turing-wavelength, 1.5 cm:asterias-rubens-clock-wavefront, 3.5 cm:asterias-rubens-elastic-buckling, 4.6 cm:asterias-rubens-morphogen-condensation, 6.0 cm:asterias-rubens-flux-canalization, 8.0 cm:asterias-rubens-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(81)90334-9>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2013.3011>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012> ;
    pk:geologicalAgeMa 0e+00 ;
